      "writtenOn": "2024-11-05T14:32:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The data type used for PCTs is a bit inconsistent. Sometimes it is a \"ComplexNumber\" composed of two doubles, other times it is 4 bytes. We would propose a third option for all cases, the IqSample composed of two signed 12bit integers, similar to the HCI format, avoiding conversions, but i am not sure if that can be expressed neatly in AIDL.\n\nSee also\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/3322440/6/bluetooth/ranging/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/ranging/ModeTwoData.aidl#39",
      "revId": "a3398e5852e8fd4d5330c38a1cb32544ed202c53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
