        "id": 1583276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-05T18:39:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. nullable will be removed, it was here as an AIDL bug which can not set default value.\n2. I use the original 4 bytes as HCI. as the value is different from the mode 2. \nthe tonePct was 3 bytes, but the packetPct is 4 bytes with the definition of unavailable(0xFFFFFFFF). if we change it to the I/Q sample. it will lose the \u0027unavailable\u0027 definition.\nI\u0027m debating it too. should it be converted at BT host?\nwith AIDL, you can not have a 12bit integers, BT stack have to convert it.\none idea in my mind is to define a structure; and BT stack will do the conversion.\nPtcIQSample {\nint iSample;\nint qsample;\nbool isAvailable \u003d true;\n}\n\nAlso, I don\u0027t like the previous ComplexNumber(double) for tonePct. I\u0027m going to change them as \u0027interger\u0027, so it conforms to the spec; vendors can do normalize or get the dBm by themselves",
      "parentUuid": "25ec95ce_c0cc55a0",
      "revId": "a3398e5852e8fd4d5330c38a1cb32544ed202c53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
